## RVfpgaEL2 SoC - Nexys A7 I2C Peripheral Example

This repository provides an **I2C peripheral example** for the **VeeRwolf EL2 SoC** adapted to the **Nexys A7** board.  
It demonstrates how to connect an **I2C core** to the SoC using the **Wishbone bus**, enabling I2C communication via the **Pmod JD** port.  

The I2C controller is memory-mapped at address **`0x80003200`**, allowing software access through standard read/write operations.  
The I2C lines are routed to **Pmod JD pins JD3 (G3)** and **JD4 (G1)**, forming an **I2C PMOD interface** for external device communication.

The main repository can be found [here](https://github.com/Kitsudora/RVFPGA-3-0-Local-Copy).

